{"entryType": "UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)", "primaryAccession": "Q3A9J4", "uniProtkbId": "GRDB_CARHZ", "entryAudit": {"firstPublicDate": "2008-02-26", "lastAnnotationUpdateDate": "2026-01-28", "lastSequenceUpdateDate": "2008-02-26", "entryVersion": 81, "sequenceVersion": 2}, "annotationScore": 3.0, "organism": {"scientificName": "Carboxydothermus hydrogenoformans (strain ATCC BAA-161 / DSM 6008 / Z-2901)", "taxonId": 246194, "lineage": ["Bacteria", "Bacillati", "Bacillota", "Clostridia", "Thermoanaerobacterales", "Thermoanaerobacteraceae", "Carboxydothermus"]}, "proteinExistence": "3: Inferred from homology", "proteinDescription": {"recommendedName": {"fullName": {"value": "Glycine reductase complex component B subunit gamma"}, "ecNumbers": [{"value": "1.21.4.2"}]}, "alternativeNames": [{"fullName": {"value": "Selenoprotein PB gamma"}}]}, "genes": [{"geneName": {"value": "grdB"}, "orderedLocusNames": [{"value": "CHY_2393"}]}], "comments": [{"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250"}], "value": "In the first step of glycine reductase, the substrate is bound to component PB via a Schiff base intermediate. Then the PB-activated substrate is nucleophilically attacked by the selenol anion of component PA to transform it to a carboxymethylated selenoether and the respective amine. By action of component PC, acetyl phosphate is formed, leaving component PA in its oxidized state. Finally component PA becomes reduced by the thioredoxin system to start a new catalytic cycle of reductive deamination (By similarity)"}], "commentType": "FUNCTION"}, {"commentType": "CATALYTIC ACTIVITY", "reaction": {"name": "acetyl phosphate + [thioredoxin]-disulfide + NH4(+) + H2O = [thioredoxin]-dithiol + glycine + phosphate + H(+)", "reactionCrossReferences": [{"database": "Rhea", "id": "RHEA:12232"}, {"database": "Rhea", "id": "RHEA-COMP:10698"}, {"database": "Rhea", "id": "RHEA-COMP:10700"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:15377"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:15378"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:22191"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:28938"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:29950"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:43474"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:50058"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:57305"}], "ecNumber": "1.21.4.2"}}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250"}], "value": "Heterohexamer of two alpha, two beta and two gamma subunits. Component of the glycine reductase complex, together with components A and C. PB is substrate specific (By similarity)"}], "commentType": "SUBUNIT"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305"}], "value": "Belongs to the GrdB/GrdF/GrdH family"}], "commentType": "SIMILARITY"}], "features": [{"type": "Chain", "location": {"start": {"value": 1, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 435, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "Glycine reductase complex component B subunit gamma", "featureId": "PRO_0000318647"}, {"type": "Active site", "location": {"start": {"value": 350, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 350, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": ""}, {"type": "Non-standard residue", "location": {"start": {"value": 350, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 350, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "Selenocysteine"}], "keywords": [{"id": "KW-0560", "category": "Molecular function", "name": "Oxidoreductase"}, {"id": "KW-1185", "category": "Technical term", "name": "Reference proteome"}, {"id": "KW-0712", "category": "Coding sequence diversity", "name": "Selenocysteine"}], "references": [{"referenceNumber": 1, "citation": {"id": "16311624", "citationType": "journal article", "authors": ["Wu M.", "Ren Q.", "Durkin A.S.", "Daugherty S.C.", "Brinkac L.M.", "Dodson R.J.", "Madupu R.", "Sullivan S.A.", "Kolonay J.F.", "Nelson W.C.", "Tallon L.J.", "Jones K.M.", "Ulrich L.E.", "Gonzalez J.M.", "Zhulin I.B.", "Robb F.T.", "Eisen J.A."], "citationCrossReferences": [{"database": "PubMed", "id": "16311624"}, {"database": "DOI", "id": "10.137